WEBVTT

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:50.040
<b>Konohana Kitan</b>

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:55.050
<b>Episode 8: 
Transient Guests</b>

00:02:03.750 --> 00:02:04.720
Um...

00:02:11.130 --> 00:02:12.080
Um...

00:02:12.610 --> 00:02:15.020
Are you all right?

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:32.510
Um...

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:36.100
Are you ill or something?

00:02:37.250 --> 00:02:38.600
Kind of.

00:02:39.140 --> 00:02:41.120
I was shipwrecked.

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:42.280
Shipwrecked?!

00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:46.850
The ship I was on capsized in a storm.

00:02:47.450 --> 00:02:51.090
I grabbed on to a piece of wood, 
and I was carried for days.

00:02:52.190 --> 00:02:56.140
When I came to, I was 
washed up on this shore.

00:02:58.250 --> 00:03:03.890
I only have a manju, but please, have it.

00:03:07.330 --> 00:03:08.490
It's fine.

00:03:08.490 --> 00:03:10.240
I'm kidding about the shipwreck.

00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:11.900
You are?!

00:03:12.310 --> 00:03:13.910
What a relief!

00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:16.600
Yeah.

00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:18.280
Storms don't bother me.

00:03:18.280 --> 00:03:19.800
I'm a mermaid.

00:03:20.490 --> 00:03:22.540
You're a mermaid?

00:03:22.540 --> 00:03:23.770
Yeah.

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:26.060
I got separated from my friends.

00:03:26.060 --> 00:03:27.850
I'm looking for them right now.

00:03:28.230 --> 00:03:31.780
I'm sure your friends must be worried.

00:03:32.790 --> 00:03:36.700
If you wouldn't mind, 
shall I help you look for them?

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:42.320
Mermaids!

00:03:42.490 --> 00:03:44.450
Mermaids!

00:03:44.710 --> 00:03:46.900
Are you here?

00:03:50.110 --> 00:03:51.980
What's the deal with this?

00:03:52.350 --> 00:03:55.250
Th-That's my tail. Why?

00:03:56.040 --> 00:03:58.070
Why do you have that thing on?

00:04:00.710 --> 00:04:06.250
Actually, I don't know 
what it's used for, either.

00:04:08.980 --> 00:04:11.760
Sorry. That was a weird thing to ask.

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:16.910
You're not even lying.

00:04:19.160 --> 00:04:20.080
Huh?

00:04:20.710 --> 00:04:23.230
It's nothing, cat girl.

00:04:23.650 --> 00:04:25.860
I'm not a cat!

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:27.070
I'm a fox!

00:04:28.220 --> 00:04:31.290
M-Mermaids! Are you—

00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:31.620
I lied about being a mermaid, too.

00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:33.450
You did?!

00:04:33.450 --> 00:04:36.040
I'm not looking for my friends, either.

00:04:36.410 --> 00:04:38.450
I don't have any friends.

00:04:39.780 --> 00:04:43.250
Everyone hates me, because I'm a liar.

00:04:45.340 --> 00:04:47.910
You always tell such childish lies.

00:04:47.910 --> 00:04:50.300
You're just looking for attention, aren't you?

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:53.130
I don't get along with my mother,

00:04:53.470 --> 00:04:57.100
and my father's a stubborn workaholic.

00:04:57.780 --> 00:05:01.260
No one listens to me at
school these days, either,

00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:03.910
because I lie about everything.

00:05:04.730 --> 00:05:08.560
No one listens to my lies anymore.

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:12.450
But when I stop lying,

00:05:13.910 --> 00:05:18.290
reality is so boring that it's painful.

00:05:19.370 --> 00:05:20.870
Is it?

00:05:21.820 --> 00:05:25.900
I work as an attendant at an inn.

00:05:25.900 --> 00:05:28.180
I get to meet all kinds 
of guests all the time.

00:05:28.180 --> 00:05:30.070
Every day is exciting.

00:05:31.580 --> 00:05:35.390
That's because you have a job that you like.

00:05:35.680 --> 00:05:38.680
I don't have dreams 
for my future or anything.

00:05:38.680 --> 00:05:41.550
Dreams for your future?

00:05:42.580 --> 00:05:44.650
Is there anything you like?

00:05:48.370 --> 00:05:51.470
I used to like picture books as a kid.

00:05:53.880 --> 00:05:57.310
And I liked drawing.

00:05:59.920 --> 00:06:01.960
That's wonderful.

00:06:01.960 --> 00:06:06.760
But I wasn't so good that I wanted 
to become an artist or anything.

00:06:13.760 --> 00:06:16.390
I'd just go to school every day,

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:19.560
and when I grew up, I'd go to work.

00:06:20.310 --> 00:06:24.160
It's the same thing day in and day out.

00:06:26.040 --> 00:06:29.180
No... Never mind.

00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:33.070
Sorry for deceiving you, fox girl.

00:06:44.260 --> 00:06:46.590
You didn't deceive me.

00:06:47.710 --> 00:06:51.350
You gave me back the manju.

00:06:52.020 --> 00:06:53.420
The manju?

00:06:53.770 --> 00:06:59.760
To deceive someone is to take something 
from them or to hurt them by lying.

00:07:00.450 --> 00:07:03.730
Your stories are fun.

00:07:03.730 --> 00:07:12.830
In just one day, I got to meet a shipwrecked 
wanderer, a lost mermaid, and you.

00:07:14.010 --> 00:07:15.560
Fun?

00:07:15.560 --> 00:07:16.440
Yes.

00:07:18.770 --> 00:07:20.720
Guys! Guys!

00:07:20.720 --> 00:07:23.360
I just a saw an alien over there!

00:07:23.790 --> 00:07:25.710
Look! A UFO!

00:07:26.480 --> 00:07:27.730
I saw it!

00:07:27.730 --> 00:07:29.660
Huh? I couldn't see it.

00:07:29.660 --> 00:07:31.790
I hope it comes back.

00:07:32.410 --> 00:07:37.890
Yeah, when I was a kid, 
it was fun, even if it was a lie.

00:07:39.370 --> 00:07:43.480
A dull reality, where every 
question is answered for you...

00:07:44.190 --> 00:07:48.300
But fantasies and daydreams 
are all a part of reality, too.

00:07:52.510 --> 00:07:56.650
I wish I had someone like you around me.

00:07:57.060 --> 00:07:58.790
You do.

00:08:00.560 --> 00:08:04.080
You have someone who enjoys your stories.

00:08:04.860 --> 00:08:07.570
Someone who needs you.

00:08:07.570 --> 00:08:08.770
I promise.

00:08:12.020 --> 00:08:17.480
Just like how I didn't know what friendship 
was until I met the people I care about.

00:08:19.410 --> 00:08:25.320
Please share your fun 
stories with more people.

00:08:43.370 --> 00:08:44.700
Matsumoto-san!

00:08:45.380 --> 00:08:46.790
Matsumoto-san!

00:08:47.570 --> 00:08:48.910
Matsumoto-san!

00:08:48.910 --> 00:08:50.290
Are you okay?

00:08:52.150 --> 00:08:54.220
You're not hurt, are you?

00:08:54.660 --> 00:08:55.640
No...

00:08:56.860 --> 00:08:57.580
Who are you?

00:08:57.580 --> 00:08:59.740
It's me, your classmate, Tanabe!

00:08:59.740 --> 00:09:02.360
I sit right in front of you!

00:09:03.290 --> 00:09:05.640
<i>Oh, yeah. That's right.</i>

00:09:05.640 --> 00:09:07.890
You scared me.

00:09:07.890 --> 00:09:10.960
You've been staying home from school lately,

00:09:10.960 --> 00:09:12.980
so I came to bring you hand-outs, and...

00:09:19.490 --> 00:09:22.520
I thought my heart was going to stop!

00:09:24.630 --> 00:09:25.850
Sorry.

00:09:25.850 --> 00:09:27.360
There were flying fish.

00:09:28.610 --> 00:09:33.050
I wanted to see if I could catch one,

00:09:33.050 --> 00:09:34.290
and I fell.

00:09:34.660 --> 00:09:36.940
Then I swam back here.

00:09:41.510 --> 00:09:42.750
Say what?

00:09:42.750 --> 00:09:43.890
That's hilarious.

00:09:45.030 --> 00:09:46.200
Hilarious?

00:09:47.190 --> 00:09:48.900
You do.

00:09:48.900 --> 00:09:51.730
You probably just haven't met them yet.

00:09:52.070 --> 00:09:54.900
But I'm glad you're alive.

00:10:03.840 --> 00:10:06.900
Maybe I was bewitched by a fox.

00:10:07.160 --> 00:10:08.560
Say what?

00:10:08.560 --> 00:10:10.630
Hey, listen to this.

00:10:10.630 --> 00:10:13.150
This dream I just had...

00:10:27.830 --> 00:10:29.740
That kid's not from this town.

00:10:30.280 --> 00:10:33.840
People sometimes wander into this side.

00:10:34.240 --> 00:10:35.150
Huh?

00:10:35.900 --> 00:10:38.060
So she did, too?

00:10:38.660 --> 00:10:42.600
They wander in and out 
without even knowing it.

00:10:42.930 --> 00:10:45.020
He'll eventually find his way back.

00:10:52.110 --> 00:10:53.370
What are those? Mice?

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:56.280
Gotcha!

00:10:56.730 --> 00:10:57.670
Ow!

00:10:57.670 --> 00:11:00.630
Hey! No picking on girls.

00:11:00.850 --> 00:11:03.190
Let me go!

00:11:01.670 --> 00:11:03.710
What's this shrimp of a guest doing here?

00:11:03.710 --> 00:11:05.910
I think that's enough...

00:11:03.980 --> 00:11:07.100
If he were a guest, I would have 
stopped you before you hit him.

00:11:08.990 --> 00:11:12.270
What's the problem? 
I wanted to play with her.

00:11:12.540 --> 00:11:14.970
This is Sakura's job.

00:11:15.540 --> 00:11:18.800
She's not like you rich kids 
who don't need to work.

00:11:18.800 --> 00:11:19.200
Ow!

00:11:20.430 --> 00:11:24.010
I'm going to do great work 
when I grow up, too!

00:11:24.010 --> 00:11:25.660
That's what everyone tells me!

00:11:26.060 --> 00:11:26.990
Everyone?

00:11:27.210 --> 00:11:29.700
Dad, Mom, Takahashi-san...

00:11:29.700 --> 00:11:32.160
Who's Takahashi-san?

00:11:32.160 --> 00:11:34.590
I'm a chosen child.

00:11:35.050 --> 00:11:41.050
"You're talented, Kaito. You might be 
even greater than your dad one day."

00:11:41.050 --> 00:11:44.840
That's how I know I'll be way more useful 
to people than that job will make her.

00:11:45.860 --> 00:11:47.070
Kaito-san...

00:11:49.810 --> 00:11:53.900
Don't you think it's sad for 
someone who's going to do

00:11:53.900 --> 00:11:58.780
great things in the future to 
look down on other people's work?

00:11:59.720 --> 00:12:01.180
Wow, that's rare.

00:12:01.180 --> 00:12:02.760
I've never seen Yuzu angry.

00:12:03.270 --> 00:12:05.730
She's angry? I can't tell!

00:12:08.470 --> 00:12:09.780
I'm sorry.

00:12:10.590 --> 00:12:11.960
Kaito!

00:12:12.670 --> 00:12:14.080
Mom's calling.

00:12:14.080 --> 00:12:15.070
See you again.

00:12:15.960 --> 00:12:17.330
"Again"?

00:12:17.330 --> 00:12:19.100
He plans on coming back?

00:12:33.190 --> 00:12:34.600
He vanished.

00:12:36.320 --> 00:12:40.770
I must finally be losing my mind.

00:12:44.810 --> 00:12:47.000
Kaito, are you awake?

00:12:47.400 --> 00:12:49.990
Want to go for a walk with Mom and Dad?

00:12:55.250 --> 00:12:57.460
Yay! I win!

00:12:58.420 --> 00:13:01.290
You've gotten so fast, Kaito.

00:13:01.290 --> 00:13:04.520
Yes, you've grown so big.

00:13:05.880 --> 00:13:07.830
It went by so fast.

00:13:10.700 --> 00:13:13.230
Why are you crying, Dad?

00:13:18.020 --> 00:13:19.240
It's Takahashi-san!

00:13:19.240 --> 00:13:20.270
Hey.

00:13:21.090 --> 00:13:22.870
Let's play!

00:13:23.430 --> 00:13:25.430
Kaito, how have you been?

00:13:25.430 --> 00:13:28.200
Hey, Takahashi-san, Mom and Dad said...

00:13:28.200 --> 00:13:31.110
Have you said goodbye to Mom and Dad yet?

00:13:34.250 --> 00:13:38.200
Kaito, study hard and become truly great.

00:13:38.490 --> 00:13:41.720
Find happiness with your new family!

00:13:50.430 --> 00:13:52.340
Did you find something?

00:13:53.080 --> 00:13:54.410
Kaito-san!

00:13:54.920 --> 00:13:56.650
What's wrong?

00:13:57.640 --> 00:14:00.190
I ran away from home.

00:14:00.500 --> 00:14:01.590
You ran away?

00:14:02.910 --> 00:14:04.420
I hate this place!

00:14:04.420 --> 00:14:06.170
I want to go home!

00:14:06.170 --> 00:14:07.910
You can't.

00:14:07.910 --> 00:14:11.400
They weren't your real parents.

00:14:12.460 --> 00:14:16.120
I can't go home to Mom

00:14:16.120 --> 00:14:18.440
because I'm not her real kid.

00:14:19.970 --> 00:14:25.870
We're all studying so we can 
do great work helping people.

00:14:26.360 --> 00:14:29.340
We're all chosen children.

00:14:29.880 --> 00:14:34.050
I don't have the freedom to choose.

00:14:35.730 --> 00:14:37.150
Kaito-san...

00:14:37.780 --> 00:14:40.680
Onee-chan, run away with me.

00:14:41.640 --> 00:14:44.950
I heard that, you brat. Now you're 
just being manipulative!

00:14:44.950 --> 00:14:45.880
Go home!

00:14:45.880 --> 00:14:46.860
No, no!

00:14:46.860 --> 00:14:48.570
I'm never going back!

00:14:48.030 --> 00:14:50.220
I'm never going home!

00:14:50.990 --> 00:14:52.030
What the?

00:14:52.470 --> 00:14:55.210
It's past your checkout date.

00:14:55.210 --> 00:14:56.370
Enough is enough.

00:14:56.370 --> 00:14:58.210
I have money.

00:14:58.210 --> 00:15:02.430
So how much do you want, forehead-ears?

00:15:02.430 --> 00:15:04.120
Forehead-ears?!

00:15:04.120 --> 00:15:06.260
Again, that's not the point!

00:15:06.260 --> 00:15:08.140
Ren, I'll take this.

00:15:09.660 --> 00:15:10.750
Okay.

00:15:11.720 --> 00:15:16.170
With all due respect, what you call "money"

00:15:16.170 --> 00:15:20.050
is nothing but waste paper in this world.

00:15:23.010 --> 00:15:24.480
I see.

00:15:24.480 --> 00:15:30.160
When I woke up after the accident, 
I couldn't figure out why I was here.

00:15:31.100 --> 00:15:34.280
I see... So this is the afterlife.

00:15:34.280 --> 00:15:36.990
Oh, no. You're still alive.

00:15:36.990 --> 00:15:39.240
So please go home already.

00:15:39.240 --> 00:15:41.580
I was about to die!

00:15:41.580 --> 00:15:43.800
Show some kindness.

00:15:44.060 --> 00:15:47.590
It seems Hell didn't want you just yet.

00:15:47.590 --> 00:15:48.950
Try again next time.

00:15:48.950 --> 00:15:51.440
You say that like I just 
failed a job interview.

00:15:51.440 --> 00:15:53.200
And really, "Hell"?

00:15:54.270 --> 00:15:59.400
I can never return to my old life, 
even if I do go back now.

00:16:03.910 --> 00:16:06.230
You don't want to go home, either, mister?

00:16:06.230 --> 00:16:08.030
You're just like me.

00:16:08.590 --> 00:16:10.850
Up and up!

00:16:11.440 --> 00:16:13.150
I see.

00:16:13.370 --> 00:16:15.710
So that's why you ran away.

00:16:16.260 --> 00:16:20.150
I thought I could become 
anything when I grew up.

00:16:20.670 --> 00:16:24.620
My future was fixed on a track 
that someone else had set up.

00:16:25.130 --> 00:16:27.940
That's a sophisticated way to say it.

00:16:30.090 --> 00:16:31.590
Listen, kid.

00:16:32.720 --> 00:16:38.930
I started out as a truck driver, and ended up 
as the president of a small transport company.

00:16:39.830 --> 00:16:42.320
I had an amazing wife and kid.

00:16:42.320 --> 00:16:46.210
Life wasn't perfectly smooth sailing, 
but I couldn't complain about it.

00:16:47.460 --> 00:16:53.590
But in just one accident, 
my life was turned upside-down.

00:16:57.220 --> 00:17:00.760
In the end, we're all dancing 
on the palm of God's hand.

00:17:01.520 --> 00:17:04.680
You're healthy and able-bodied, kid.

00:17:04.980 --> 00:17:06.770
You have hope and a future.

00:17:07.660 --> 00:17:09.710
Those are all things I don't have.

00:17:11.250 --> 00:17:15.030
But you have a family.

00:17:16.280 --> 00:17:20.750
I wasn't my mom and dad's real child.

00:17:22.260 --> 00:17:24.200
We weren't a real family.

00:17:23.610 --> 00:17:25.670
You're just like me, then.

00:17:27.170 --> 00:17:31.030
My only daughter is 
my wife's kid from before.

00:17:31.380 --> 00:17:35.580
She was so cold and distant to me at first.

00:17:35.580 --> 00:17:39.630
Seriously, why are young girls like that?

00:17:39.630 --> 00:17:41.790
Oh, are you really asking me?

00:17:42.020 --> 00:17:46.270
She wouldn't accept me as her
family for the longest time.

00:17:46.640 --> 00:17:48.290
Is that why you don't want to go home?

00:17:48.290 --> 00:17:49.460
Don't be stupid!

00:17:49.460 --> 00:17:52.450
I'm not <i>that</i> petty!

00:17:52.450 --> 00:17:54.500
I raised her as my own!

00:17:54.500 --> 00:17:58.190
I paid a ton in tuition so she could 
go to an art school or something!

00:17:58.190 --> 00:18:00.550
She's moved out now and doing what she loves!

00:18:01.230 --> 00:18:04.120
Why don't you want to go home, then?

00:18:04.120 --> 00:18:06.260
She's probably waiting for you.

00:18:08.080 --> 00:18:09.380
What's so funny?

00:18:10.280 --> 00:18:12.860
How can I just go home now?

00:18:13.200 --> 00:18:16.970
We became family with the promise 
that I'd make them happy.

00:18:17.970 --> 00:18:21.330
I know I'll be a burden to them from now on.

00:18:21.660 --> 00:18:24.140
How am I supposed to face them?

00:18:26.190 --> 00:18:30.350
Please, dear, won't you wake up now?

00:18:30.970 --> 00:18:36.220
I served them well, as a man and as a father.

00:18:36.650 --> 00:18:41.030
I can end it now and call it a good life.

00:18:41.030 --> 00:18:43.000
Don't you think, fox lady?

00:18:43.510 --> 00:18:46.790
In the end, we're all dancing 
on the palm of God's hand.

00:18:46.790 --> 00:18:49.030
Isn't that what you said?

00:18:49.410 --> 00:18:51.860
You're trying too hard to look good.

00:18:52.950 --> 00:18:55.450
You sound like my wife.

00:18:55.450 --> 00:18:59.270
Indeed, I could hear your wife's grumbling.

00:19:00.270 --> 00:19:04.490
She married you knowing 
that's the kind of man you are.

00:19:04.800 --> 00:19:08.010
You're the only one who thinks 
they haven't figured you out.

00:19:08.350 --> 00:19:11.570
Just surrender and go back 
to the palm of your wife's hand.

00:19:13.580 --> 00:19:16.990
Damn it! I'm never coming back here!

00:19:16.990 --> 00:19:17.650
Of course.

00:19:17.650 --> 00:19:19.500
Thank you for your patronage.

00:19:20.620 --> 00:19:22.410
Be well, kid.

00:19:23.090 --> 00:19:25.630
We share an odd bond.

00:19:26.860 --> 00:19:28.910
I'll see you around.

00:19:35.220 --> 00:19:36.820
I'm going home.

00:19:36.820 --> 00:19:39.500
Do you feel better about your situation now?

00:19:45.090 --> 00:19:48.290
I don't know about my future or anything,

00:19:48.290 --> 00:19:53.490
but I want to study hard and be able to help.

00:19:59.010 --> 00:20:03.520
I told you, my hair hasn't grown yet!

00:20:03.520 --> 00:20:05.340
Get back here!

00:20:06.310 --> 00:20:07.110
You kids!

00:20:07.110 --> 00:20:09.600
I don't mind you having fun, 
but don't wander into a guest room.

00:20:10.230 --> 00:20:14.940
Speaking of wandering in, 
remember that little boy?

00:20:14.940 --> 00:20:16.570
What little boy?

00:20:18.680 --> 00:20:19.740
Yuzu-chan.

00:20:21.200 --> 00:20:23.510
Kaito-san, is that you?

00:20:23.790 --> 00:20:27.410
You've grown so small since 
I last saw you, Yuzu-chan.

00:20:27.410 --> 00:20:30.460
It's you who grew, Kaito-san.

00:20:30.460 --> 00:20:32.250
Are you doing well?

00:20:32.250 --> 00:20:35.200
Yeah. I have a new family.

00:20:37.690 --> 00:20:39.740
It's time for Dad to leave.

00:20:39.740 --> 00:20:40.740
I have to go back.

00:20:43.240 --> 00:20:45.110
Bye-bye, Yuzu-chan.

00:20:47.770 --> 00:20:49.890
"Bye-bye," huh?

00:20:49.890 --> 00:20:51.870
Not "See you again"?

00:20:52.230 --> 00:20:53.640
You do remember him.

00:20:54.120 --> 00:20:58.580
He must have found 
what he was looking for.

00:21:01.060 --> 00:21:02.120
Kaito.

00:21:04.740 --> 00:21:05.700
Kaito.

00:21:06.090 --> 00:21:08.040
Are you awake, Kaito?

00:21:08.040 --> 00:21:09.880
Let's go shopping.

00:21:11.650 --> 00:21:12.740
How cute.

00:21:13.110 --> 00:21:16.180
Are these from when Kaito was a puppy?

00:21:16.180 --> 00:21:19.560
The volunteers took lots of pictures for us.

00:21:20.310 --> 00:21:22.520
He couldn't get used to 
the training center at first.

00:21:22.520 --> 00:21:25.160
We weren't sure he'd make the cut.

00:21:25.540 --> 00:21:27.550
But he grew up amazingly well.

00:21:28.140 --> 00:21:35.110
My husband had been completely shut-in 
ever since he lost his eyesight in the accident,

00:21:35.520 --> 00:21:39.600
but he seems truly happy 
since Kaito's been here.

00:21:40.480 --> 00:21:43.440
<b>The Fox by the Sea</b>

00:21:40.910 --> 00:21:45.540
It's been lonely since our daughter moved out,

00:21:43.440 --> 00:21:45.530
<b>By: Matsumoto Rei</b>

00:21:46.210 --> 00:21:49.310
but we have a beautiful young boy now.

00:21:50.590 --> 00:21:53.810
All right, buddy. I'm counting on you.

00:21:57.580 --> 00:21:58.350
Go!

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:39.970
<b>Next Episode: 
Evanescent...</b>
